Subject: The nursery reconcile reads the time-stamp counter only when QJS_Y_STATS is set

What this does
  - quickjs.c: `y_tsc()` returns 0 unless QJS_Y_STATS is in the environment; the environment is read once.

Why we need it
  Every reconcile and every young collection read the counter several times for a statistics report nobody asked for.

Soundness
  The counters feed only the QJS_Y_STATS report; nothing else reads them.

Failure modes
  Without QJS_Y_STATS the cycle columns of the report are zero.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -4675 +4675,2 @@
-static inline uint64_t y_tsc(void) { return __builtin_ia32_rdtsc(); }
+static int y_tsc_on = -1;
+static inline uint64_t y_tsc(void) { if (unlikely(y_tsc_on < 0)) y_tsc_on = getenv("QJS_Y_STATS") != NULL; return y_tsc_on ? __builtin_ia32_rdtsc() : 0; }
